{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.PairwiseChainLeadingOrder","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.LeadingOrderTraceCoefficient","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanMarkovTrace","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_kappa_three_way_reconciliation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_kappa_three_way_reconciliation","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L268-L295","doc":"**Master reconciliation of `κ = 3/16` across all three deuteron / Borromean routes:**\n1. **Route 1 (first-order `ℏ_q` chain vs deuteron):** `c₁(pp) + c₁(pn) = 3/16 = κ`, while the\n   deuteron (`pn`) alone has `c₁(pn) = 1/16 = κ/3`.\n2. **Route 1 (second-order `ε²` `|S| = 2` pair classes):** the `A = 3` intra-nucleon slope is\n   `κ = 3/16`, the deuteron cross-nucleon term is `-κ = -3/16`, and adding the nucleon–interface\n   term `+1/8` gives the net deuteron `|S| = 2` coefficient `-1/16 = -c₁(pn)`.\n3. **Route 2 (`h²` Borromean trace normalization):** standard `[2]_q² = h² + 4` gives `h²`\n   coefficient `0`, while `(√q + 1/√q)² = w² + 4` shifts the denominator from `1 + h²/4` to\n   `1 + h²/16 + O(h⁴)` and produces `κ = 1/4 - 1/16 = 3/16` (`4κ = 3/4` in Family A).\n4. **Route 3 (trefoil Seifert 2-form on `σ₁³`):** provides the framing- and dressing-invariant\n   non-abelian commutator carrier `1 · ⁅A_0, A_1⁆` (`V_{01} - V_{10} = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route3_trefoil_operator_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route3_trefoil_operator_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L251-L264","doc":"The discretized Yekutieli surface 2-form on the deuteron trefoil Seifert surface equals\nthe single handle-holonomy commutator `⁅A_0, A_1⁆` with coefficient `1`, and is invariant under\ncentral color/flavor scalar dressings `s_0, s_1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route3_trefoil_seifert_skew_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route3_trefoil_seifert_skew_unit","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L241-L249","doc":"On the genus-1 right-handed trefoil Seifert surface (`pn` 2-strand braid `σ₁³`), the\nskew intersection coefficient `V_{01} - V_{10}` is `+1`, whereas the symmetric self-linking\ndiagonal entries `V_{00} = V_{11} = -1` cancel out of `surface2Form`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route2_denominator_shift_and_family_a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route2_denominator_shift_and_family_a","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L221-L237","doc":"**Origin of `3/16` as a denominator shift, and the Family-A `4 · (3/16) = 3/4` bridge:**\n- The numerator `4 + h² = 4(1 + (1/4)h²)` contributes `+1/4` at `h²`.\n- The standard denominator `4 + h² = 4(1 + (1/4)h²)` subtracts `1/4`, leaving `1/4 - 1/4 = 0`.\n- The Yekutieli denominator `4 + w² = 4(1 + (1/16)h² + O(h⁴))` subtracts `1/16`, leaving\n  `1/4 - 1/16 = 3/16 = κ_borromean`.\n- Multiplying by the `q = 1` loop factor `4` gives `4 · (3/16) = 3/4`, the `h²` slope of\n  Family A's `linking_weight_family_a_h(h) = 5/2 + (3/4)h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route2_yekutieli_kappa_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route2_yekutieli_kappa_unique","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L206-L219","doc":"**Uniqueness of `κ_Yek = 3/16`:** for an arbitrary candidate coefficient `κ : ℚ`, the\n`w²` term of `borromeanNumOfHSq (hSqOfW w) - yekutieliDen w * (1 + κ * hSqOfW w)` is\n`(3 - 16 κ) w²`, which vanishes iff `κ = 3/16`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route2_yekutieli_h2_is_three_sixteenths","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route2_yekutieli_h2_is_three_sixteenths","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L198-L204","doc":"**Over `ℚ`:** dividing the Borromean numerator by `(√q + 1/√q)² = w² + 4` gives the quadratic\napproximation `1 + (3/16) h²` with an exact `O(w⁴) = O(h⁴)` remainder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route2_yekutieli_h2_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route2_yekutieli_h2_mul","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L186-L194","doc":"**Yekutieli / `[2]_q + 2` normalization (`w² + 4`), division-free over `R[w]`:**\nclearing `16`, the remainder `16 · V(𝓑₃) - (w² + 4) · (16 + 3 h²)` factors through `w⁴` (no `w⁰` or\n`w²` term). This is the exact algebraic reason dividing `V(𝓑₃)` by `(√q + 1/√q)² = w² + 4`\nproduces `h²` coefficient `κ_Yek = 3/16` instead of `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route2_standard_h2_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route2_standard_h2_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L178-L184","doc":"**Standard Kauffman–Jones normalization (`[2]_q² = h² + 4`):** the `h²` coefficient of\n`tr_M(β_Bor, h)` is `0` (`trM_borromean_num h - trM_borromean_den h · 1` is purely `O(h⁴)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.borromeanNumOfHSq_eq_trM_num","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.borromeanNumOfHSq_eq_trM_num","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L172-L176","doc":"Compatibility with `QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_num`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.yekutieliDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.yekutieliDen","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L169-L170","doc":"The Yekutieli / `_li_2_q_util` denominator `(√q + 1/√q)² = q + 2 + q⁻¹ = [2]_q + 2 = w² + 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.borromeanNumOfHSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.borromeanNumOfHSq","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L166-L167","doc":"The Borromean Jones numerator `4 + h² - 3h⁴ - h⁶` written as a polynomial in `hSq = h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.hSqOfW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.hSqOfW","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L162-L164","doc":"In terms of the half-step parameter `w = q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2}`, the full Hecke parameter\n`h = q - q⁻¹ = (q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2})(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})` satisfies `h² = w²(w² + 4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_deuteron_S2_reconciliation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_deuteron_S2_reconciliation","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L143-L154","doc":"On the deuteron (`pn`), the `|S| = 2` cross-nucleon term is `-κ = -3/16`, and adding the\nnucleon–interface term `+1/8 = +2/16` yields the net `|S| = 2` contribution `-1/16 = -c₁(pn)`,\nwhich combines with `|S| = 0` (`0`) and `|S| = 1` (`27/32`) to give `c₂(pn) = 25/32`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_S2_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_S2_total","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L141-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_S2_ifif","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_S2_ifif","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L140-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_S2_nif","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_S2_nif","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L139-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_S2_cross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_S2_cross","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L138-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_S2_intra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.deuteron_S2_intra","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L131-L137","doc":"Deuteron (`pn`, `Z = 1, N = 1`) second-order `|S| = 2` pair-class components from the exact\ndiagonal-insertion expansion (`c2_pair_class_decomposition_probe.py`, bean `qou-qqm4`):\n- `intra = 0` (`Z = N = 1`)\n- `cross = -3/16 = -κ` (inter-nucleon letter pairs)\n- `n-if = +1/8 = +2/16` (nucleon–interface letter pairs)\n- `if-if = 0` (only one interface letter at `A = 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_intraA3_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_intraA3_values","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L119-L129","doc":"The affine law `intra(Z, N) = (Z - N) · (3/16)` reproduces all four `A = 3` species\n(`3p`, `T`, `³He`, `3n`) and vanishes identically at `Z = N = 1` (deuteron isospin singlet/triplet\nsymmetric content `Z = N`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.intraA3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.intraA3","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L115-L117","doc":"At second order in `ε = q - 1` (bean `qou-qqm4`), the `A = 3` intra-nucleon `|S| = 2` pair-class\ncontribution is `(Z - N) · κ` with `κ(3) = 3/16`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_borromean_letter_weights_sum_to_kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_borromean_letter_weights_sum_to_kappa","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L104-L113","doc":"Why `3/16` appears in the Borromean pairwise sum: for arbitrary per-nucleon letter weights\n`(a, b)`, the three `A = 2` pair coefficients sum to `3(a + b)/16` (`pairSum_of_letters`); at the\nBorromean weights `(a, b) = (3, -2)` we have `a + b = 1`, pinning the pair sum to `3/16`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_deuteron_c1_reconciliation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_deuteron_c1_reconciliation","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L91-L102","doc":"For the deuteron (`²H`, `pn`, `Z = 1, N = 1`), the first-order trace difference coefficient\nderived from the 18-letter star sums `star_pnFree (1/8) - star_pnAtom (1/16)` is `c₁(pn) = 1/16`,\nwhich is exactly one-third of `κ = 3/16` (`c₁(pp) = 2/16` carries the other two-thirds). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_chain_He4_eq_kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_chain_He4_eq_kappa","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L84-L89","doc":"At first order in `ℏ_q`, the `⁴He` (`pp + pn + nn`) pairwise chain sum also equals `κ = 3/16`\nbecause `c₁(nn) = 0` under the Borromean intra-nucleon ordering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_chain_He3_eq_kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.route1_chain_He3_eq_kappa","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L78-L82","doc":"At first order in `ℏ_q`, the `³He` (`pp + pn`) pairwise chain sum equals `κ = 3/16`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.kappa_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKappaReconciliation.kappa_borromean","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronKappaThreeSixteenthsReconciliation.lean#L71-L74","doc":"The rational constant `κ = 3/16` shared across the Borromean pairwise chain sum,\nthe `A = 3` intra-nucleon / deuteron cross-nucleon `|S| = 2` expansion, and the\nYekutieli `(√q + 1/√q)²` Borromean `h²` extraction. ","signatureChunk":0}]}